Z||000000||dodger||03-14-2000||11:42 PM||||So I was on my way down Hwy 1 in my newly shined 86 SE last Sunday to meet my girlfriend for tennis in Carmel Valley when the V6 just stopped at Castroville. Used the cell phone to get AAA, then George Miller at the Fiero Shop. In a few hours he had my car on his trailer headed back to his shop in Hayward, some 70 miles away. I rode up with him and watched him fix it, paid (about half the usual garage rate, and none for the towing!), and drove home and to work Monday.<BR>Unbelievable service! It just doesn't happen in the world I live in! But this was the second time...<BR>   I heard about George in the forum here when I asked a tech question...Stimpy told me to look up George before I "contributed more money to the Mr. Goodwrench retirement fund".  I was quoted the going rate for a repair at a garage recommended by a friend, and George saved me about half (more than $200.00!). The only hitch was he made me join the Golden Gate Fiero Club...lol. Well I'm glad I did. I went to the last meeting and hope to make it to the Modesto Big O opening. So, Thanks Stimpy...and George!<P>C.G. Bush Jr.<BR>86 Red SE<BR>Golden Gate Fieros<BR>Watsonville<P>(and I can't wait to see that red Honda again in Seaside, it's two lanes into one up that onramp!)  <P> <BR>||||reg||7
